e\">Simp</span>.<span class=\"name\">getSimpTheoremNames</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames\">DeclTheoremNames</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the names of the theorems contributed by `declName` when it is used as a `Sym.simp`\ntheorem. A proposition contributes itself. A definition contributes its equational theorems\nand, when it is not recursive, its unfolding theorem, so that `simp [f]` unfolds `f`\napplications.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.getSimpTheoremNames","kind":"def","line":247,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.getSimpTheoremNames","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.lean#L247-L273"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames.unfold?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Simp</span>.<span class=\"name\">DeclTheoremNames</span>.<span class=\"name\">unfold?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames\">DeclTheoremNames</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The unfolding theorem `f.eq_def` of a non-recursive definition `f`, unless `thms` already\nunfolds every `f` application. It is a fallback (see `Theorem.fallback`), so that `simp [f]`\nunfolds the `f` applications not covered by the equational theorems, like `Meta.simp` does.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames.unfold?","kind":"def","line":239,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames.unfold?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.lean#L239-L239"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames.thms\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Simp</span>.<span class=\"name\">DeclTheoremNames</span>.<span class=\"name\">thms</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames\">DeclTheoremNames</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The declaration itself when it is a proposition, or the equational theorems of a definition.\nEmpty for a reducible definition, which the `Sym` preprocessing unfolds.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames.thms","kind":"def","line":233,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.DeclTheoremNames.thms","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.lean#L233-L233"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">constructor</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" hre